      "query": "{\"content\": \"P(grant) 0.08. The petition asks the Court to overrule *Jones v. United States* (1960) and hold that hearsay cannot support a search warrant. This would be a seismic shift in Fourth Amendment jurisprudence and criminal procedure, effectively eliminating the use of confidential informants and officer-to-officer hearsay for warrants. While the petition is supported by four amicus briefs and the Court requested a response (elevating its salience), the Court rarely overrules such entren",
